      "statusChangeNewStatus": "needs more information",
      "value": "We haven't yet been able to reproduce this problem internally. A test avatar containing VRChat constraints appears to load and function as expected, and switching into uploaded avatars with VRChat constraints afterwards seems to behave as expected as well.\n\nAre you able to please retest on the current open beta to see if this issue is still affecting you? If it is, please provide:\n\n- The ID of the uploaded avatar. There's no need to make this public if it's private.\n\n- The locally built avatar file for the avatar that causes constraints to break. You should be able to find this in the folder `C:\\Users\\<username>\\AppData\\LocalLow\\VRChat\\VRChat\\Avatars` - it's a .vrca file with the same name as your avatar. Please submit this file to us via https://vrch.at/support, linking to this Canny issue for context, and we'll pass the file along internally.\n\nMany thanks.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
