  "details": "this is an extension of my previous issue https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1481-vrc-constraints-cant-distinguish-transforms-with-identical-names\n\none thing I was doing that whole time was uploading test avatars since that usually is a quicker process, upon none of them working I swapped back into non test avatars only to find their constraints broken too, I found this odd as I recalled using one the previous night just fine, and I have learned that the beta also auto converts constraints in game, upon restarting my game I found all my avatars were totally fine again\n\nthat is until I swapped into a test avatar, test avatars break constraints entirely for every avatar until the game is restarted, this makes test avatars completely unusable. from constraints not attaching themselves correctly, to flat out not working at all\n\nI have found this issue is only a problem if that test avatar contained any constraints, if the test avatar is constraint free, it seems to be fine\n\nattached will be a photo of a test avatar where the top half is not constraining to the lower half at all, and a picture of another avatar where the eyes aren't working as a result",
